WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.770
Sports day was wonderful, and

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.290
I took forty photos.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.000
I want to post the best ones on

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.060
the school page tonight.

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.900
But which ones?

6
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.120
And who will see them?

7
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.080
Today: how to share pupils’ photos safely,

8
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.720
and keep your own accounts professional.

9
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.150
Start with consent.

10
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.870
Parents agree in writing, usually on

11
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.830
the school’s consent form, before

12
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.510
their child’s photo goes online.

13
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.100
If a parent says no, that

14
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.460
child isn’t in the photo.

15
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.600
And older pupils deserve to be asked too.

16
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.880
A photo can say more than you think.

17
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.160
A full name under a face.

18
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.200
The school’s name on a

19
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.720
jumper, or on the gate.

20
00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:47.490
A list of names on the board behind.

21
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.150
And the photo file itself may

22
00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.410
store where it was taken.

23
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.880
So here’s the rule.

24
00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.350
Post groups, or pupils from

25
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.770
behind or far away.

26
00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.650
Never put full names next to faces.

27
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.200
Check the background before you post.

28
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.710
And turn off location tags in your camera.

29
00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.230
Small details add up, like

30
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.390
pieces of a puzzle.

31
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.600
A uniform, a bus stop, a

32
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.380
birthday, a pet’s name.

33
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.200
One piece tells a stranger nothing.

34
00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.050
Together, they tell them where a

35
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.670
child will be, and when.

36
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:25.470
Quick check!

37
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.940
Here are three sports-day photos.

38
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.830
Which one is safest to post

39
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:33.870
on the school page?

40
00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.440
The team from behind, with no names.

41
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.100
You still share the joy of the day, but no

42
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.580
stranger learns who, where or when.

43
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.240
Send close-ups only to each

44
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.660
child’s own family.

45
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.400
Now your own accounts.

46
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.260
Keep your personal profile private.

47
00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.530
Don’t accept pupils as friends on it.

48
00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.970
Talk to pupils and parents through

49
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.550
the school’s official channels.

50
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.780
And search your own name once a

51
00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.600
term, to see what others see.

52
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.760
Sometimes a fake page

53
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.280
pretends to be the school.

54
00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.410
It asks parents to pay next term’s

55
00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.930
fees to a new number, by Friday.

56
00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.040
Report the page to the platform.

57
00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.920
Then warn parents on the school’s

58
00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.240
official channel: the school never

59
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.360
changes its payment number in a post.

60
00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:28.290
In the lab, look at six

61
00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.290
harmless-looking posts by a pupil, and

62
00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.270
see what a stranger can piece together.

63
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.620
Then make her profile safer.

64
00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:37.510
Your turn.

65
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.140
A pupil sends you a friend request

66
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.520
on your personal account.

67
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.170
Accept it, or not?

68
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.920
Don’t accept: keep your personal

69
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.240
and school accounts apart.

70
00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.220
Remember: consent first, groups with

71
00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.100
no names, check the background, and

72
00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.680
keep your own profile private.

73
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.910
Try it in class tomorrow: describe three

74
00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.110
photos, or draw them on the board.

75
00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.680
Pupils find every detail that gives away

76
00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.800
who, where or when, and suggest how to

77
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.440
make each one safe to share.
